  "body": "The new Rust bridge derives affine consequences after solver assignments and removes each conditional generation before rollback. A separate BigUint/LIFO checker binds the exact premises and invokes the frozen coefficient checker. Every original equation remains. The disabled fork matches the old engine's complete answers, decisions, counters and schedule on33 fixed systems. Native PCC-20261116-0c76bf; native post-call reader PCC-20261116-10062c; all unsigned/unverified. [pcc:unverified]\n\nOn28 curve inputs the baseline returns15Root/13Unsupported; the enabled bridge returns13Root/15cumulative-modeled-reservation caps. All13 enabled curve roots keep their original node counts; two indexed baseline roots become caps. One synthetic Fp29 control changes3to2nodes and is reported separately. Shorter capped traces are never gains or absence certificates. Full cold work, actual live storage and checker/allocator/replay costs remain open; no performance or scaling admission. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe inspected two-page [report](https://github.com/isogeny-labs/crypto/blob/lane/curve25519-affine/research/curve25519_torus_native_20261115/reports/branch-affine-v1/report.pdf), editable lifetime diagram, native-recorded plot/data, protocol, reproduction and criteria-application record are included. Core98inputs/five archives/35compiled bindings remain distinct from the separately frozen post-call reader. Release library controls/fmt/build/strict all-target Clippy pass locally. Historical Python status grouping is excluded from acceptance; the Rust reader hashes247 raw members and recomputes the totals. All failures and whitespace advisories remain byte-preserved. Report PCC-20261116-49751a. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe real280300-byte whole raw archive is staged for the maintained trusted artifact-autofix uploader, SHA-256 `5332de1c3b6981ab664cc6e71b1c162996ac7ef812a572a382af5382b27896ad`. Require the actual subsequent manifest/upload receipt; tracked data is not upload success. The previous static146256-byte payload remains separately bound to `ef5b561a184672f36ac9c2e12963f23d14d56aa731ea6e3d79f68968b3e2a875`. No credentials, policy/exemption or workflow change. See PUBLISHING.md. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThis follow-on uses a pinned source-context review base, commit345652eb. Main d06c4a8 lacks51 frozen predecessor dependency inputs and root AGENTS; the complete buildable context remains at that commit. This PR must wait for main dependency integration and then fresh gate/size/artifacts/reviews; do not merge it into the feature base to avoid main gates. Context/candidate use the same legitimate upstream artifact policy. Predecessors4447 and4456 merged externally; partial publication-only closure episodes E-11e95656eb81/E-e803d1d21ce1 and matching outcomes are included. Canonical owners still need to reconcile nine omitted published registrations. Only this task's genuinely unpublished claims were registered; no published rows were replayed/rechained. [pcc:unverified]\n\nSources: Soos/Nohl/Castelluccia2009 section3.2 pp248–249 (GF2 quiescent Gaussian reasoning and backtracking), Shoup NTBv2 section14.4, and the repository's static/worklist predecessors. KB unavailable; primary sources read and no novelty claimed for this classical hybrid. Next is a bounded reversible component with storage/checker accounting. No successor campaign is scheduled. Canonical cost/exponent charts and benchmarks remain unchanged because no admitted performance datum is added; original huge-base/yield/selection/kernel/recovery obligations remain open. [pcc:unverified]\n",
